  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: PhysDisc 3
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "A research team has identified a new compound that looks promising in
    the lab, but based on its properties, it may require a complex delivery method
    that wouldn\u2019t be easy for patients to manage long-term. As a physician,
    this raises concerns\u2014you\u2019ve always been told that, even in the early
    stages of research, part of the physician\u2019s role is to help researchers
    focus on treatments that are practical and realistic for patients\u2019 daily
    lives, not just effective in theory.\r\n\nIs this true or false?\r\n"
  explanation: "Even in the earliest stages of research, physicians help keep the
    focus on patients. A treatment that works in theory won\u2019t actually help
    if it\u2019s too hard for people to use in real life. By pointing out practical
    issues early in the research\u2014like whether a treatment would be too complicated,
    too invasive, or hard to keep up with\u2014physicians guide the team toward options
    that patients could realistically manage. "
  correctAnswer: True
  incorrectAnswer1: False
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Physician
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: Discovery
